import \"tailwindcss\" + custom theme tokens\n├── .env.example\n├── tsconfig.json\n└── vite.config.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key npm Packages & Verified Versions (2025–2026 Ecosystem)\n\n| Package | Recommended Version | Purpose |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `react` & `react-dom` | `^19.3.0` | Latest React with native `<ViewTransition>`, Action hooks (`useActionState`, `useOptimistic`), and type optimizations |\n| `vite` | `^8.3.0` | High-performance dev server and bundler |\n| `@tailwindcss/vite` | `^4.3.3` | Tailwind CSS v4 official Vite plugin (zero-config, CSS-first) |\n| `tailwindcss` | `^4.3.3` | Core Tailwind v4 styling engine |\n| `@supabase/supabase-js` | `^2.117.0` | Supabase Postgres client, Auth, Realtime, and Storage APIs |\n| `@tanstack/react-query` | `^5.103.0` | Server-state caching, optimistic updates, and background refetching |\n| `zustand` | `^5.0.15` | Minimalist client UI state management (active language, drawer open/close) |\n| `tesseract.js` | `^7.0.0` | WebAssembly-based client-side OCR with Web Worker support |\n| `i18next` & `react-i18next`| `^24.0.0` / `^17.0.15` | Robust internationalization framework for Hindi/English switching |\n| `i18next-browser-languagedetector` | `^8.0.0` | Automatic browser language detection with `localStorage` persistence |\n| `i18next-http-backend` | `^3.0.0` | Lazy-loads translation JSON files from `/public/locales` |\n| `qrcode.react` | `^4.2.0` | Generates SVG & Canvas QR codes for ABHA card & OPD Scan-and-Share |\n| `lucide-react` | `^1.47.0` | Comprehensive medical, alert, document, and interface icons |\n| `zod` | `^3.24.0` | Runtime schema validation for ABDM payloads, OCR parsed fields, and forms |\n| `date-fns` | `^4.1.0` | Lightweight date math and localization for Indian appointment/record dates |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Vite + Tailwind CSS v4 Setup\n\nTailwind CSS v4 replaces `tailwind.config.js` and `postcss.config.js` with a single Vite plugin and CSS-first configuration:\n\n### `vite.config.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';\nimport tailwindcss from '@tailwindcss/vite';\nimport path from 'path';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    react(),\n    tailwindcss(),\n  ],\n  resolve: {\n    alias: {\n      '@': path.resolve(__dirname, './src'),\n    },\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### `src/index.css`\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n@theme {\n  /* Medical Trust Color Palette */\n  --color-medical-primary: #0284c7;     /* Sky 600 - Reliable clinical blue */\n  --color-medical-primary-dark: #0369a1;\n  --color-medical-accent: #0d9488;      /* Teal 600 - Healing, calm teal */\n  --color-medical-surface: #f8fafc;     /* Slate 50 - Sanitary background */\n  --color-medical-card: #ffffff;\n  \n  /* Clinical Severity Palette (WCAG Compliant) */\n  --color-status-normal: #15803d;       /* Green 700 */\n  --color-status-normal-bg: #f0fdf4;\n  --color-status-warning: #b45309;      /* Amber 700 */\n  --color-status-warning-bg: #fffbeb;\n  --color-status-critical: #b91c1c;     /* Red 700 */\n  --color-status-critical-bg: #fef2f2;\n\n  --font-sans: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\n  --font-hindi: 'Noto Sans Devanagari', system-ui, sans-serif;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Supabase Client v2 Setup (Auth, Database, Storage)\n\n### `src/lib/supabase.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';\nimport type { Database } from '@/types/database.types';\n\nconst supabaseUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL;\nconst supabaseAnonKey = import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY;\n\nif (!supabaseUrl || !supabaseAnonKey) {\n  throw new Error('Missing Supabase environment variables');\n}\n\nexport const supabase = createClient<Database>(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey, {\n  auth: {\n    persistSession: true,\n    autoRefreshToken: true,\n    detectSessionInUrl: true,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Client-Side OCR Architecture (Tesseract.js in Web Worker)\n\nPrescription and diagnostic document scans must be processed client-side to ensure strict data privacy before user review and cloud sync.\n\n### Workflow:\n1. **Camera/File Upload**: Capture high-resolution image (`image/jpeg`, `image/png`).\n2. **Preprocessing (Off-Thread Canvas)**:\n   - Convert to Grayscale.\n   - Adjust contrast & brightness (stretch histogram).\n   - Optional Otsu adaptive thresholding for binarization to clean up pen ink from doctor pads.\n3. **Web Worker OCR (`tesseract.js`)**:\n   - Use `createWorker(['eng', 'hin'])` to support bilingual Indian prescriptions.\n   - Stream progress updates (`0% -> 100%`) back to UI using `aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n4. **Regex Heuristic Parser**:\n   - Extract Date, Doctor Name (`Dr. ...`), Medication names (`Rx: ...`), and Dosages (`1-0-1`, `OD`, `BD`, `TDS`).\n5. **Human-in-the-Loop Review**: Present an editable verification form prior to saving.\n\n```typescript\n// src/features/scanner/workers/ocrService.ts\nimport { createWorker } from 'tesseract.js';\n\nexport async function performOcr(imageSource: string | File, onProgress?: (p: number) => void) {\n  const worker = await createWorker('eng+hin', 1, {\n    logger: (m) => {\n      if (m.status === 'recognizing text' && onProgress) {\n        onProgress(Math.round(m.progress * 100));\n      }\n    },\n  });\n\n  const { data: { text, confidence } } = await worker.recognize(imageSource);\n  await worker.terminate();\n\n  return { text, confidence };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. India ABDM / ABHA Sandbox V3 Integration Patterns\n\nIndia’s National Health Authority (NHA) has standardized on **ABDM V3 APIs** (`https://dev.abdm.gov.in/api/hiecm/gateway/v3/`).\n\n### Architecture Rules:\n- **Never expose `CLIENT_SECRET` in frontend code.** All calls to ABDM Gateway must be proxied via Supabase Edge Functions (`/functions/v1/abdm-proxy`).\n- **Standard V3 Headers**:\n  - `Authorization: Bearer <gateway_session_token>`\n  - `X-CM-ID: sbx` (sandbox)\n  - `REQUEST-ID: <UUID-v4>`\n  - `TIMESTAMP: <ISO-8601 UTC>`\n\n### The 3 Core Milestones:\n1. **M1: ABHA Identity Management**:\n   - **Aadhaar OTP / Mobile OTP Flow**:\n     - `POST /v3/hip/enroll/request/otp` -> Patient receives OTP.\n     - `POST /v3/hip/enroll/auth/byAadhaar` -> Returns verified ABHA Profile (14-digit ABHA ID `XX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX`, ABHA Address `user@sbx`, name, gender, DOB, photo).\n   - **Scan & Share (OPD QR)**:\n     - Patient scans hospital QR code at registration counter, which passes patient demographics into the Hospital Management Information System (HMIS) queue, issuing an instant OPD slip.\n2. **M2: Health Information Provider (HIP)**:\n   - Patient Discovery: User enters mobile or ABHA -> HIP confirms match.\n   - Care Context Linking: Links specific visits (`careContextId: \"VISIT-2026-09-01\"`, `type: \"OPD_CONSULTATION\"`).\n   - Record Push: Bundles clinical records as **NRCeS FHIR R4** JSON bundles.\n3. **M3: Health Information User (HIU)**:\n   - **Consent Flow**: Request consent for longitudinal records (`hiu/consent-requests/init`).\n   - Patient approves consent in their personal ABHA app (e.g., ABHA App, Aarogya Setu).\n   - **Fidelius Encryption**: ABDM uses Diffie-Hellman Key Exchange + AES-GCM-256 for end-to-end encrypted FHIR bundle transport.\n\n---\n\n## 8. react-i18next Setup (Hindi + English)\n\n### `src/lib/i18n.ts`\n```typescript\nimport i18n from 'i18next';\nimport { initReactI18next } from 'react-i18next';\nimport LanguageDetector from 'i18next-browser-languagedetector';\nimport HttpBackend from 'i18next-http-backend';\n\ni18n\n  .use(HttpBackend)\n  .use(LanguageDetector)\n  .use(initReactI18next)\n  .init({\n    fallbackLng: 'en',\n    supportedLngs: ['en', 'hi'],\n    debug: false,\n    interpolation: {\n      escapeValue: false, // React handles XSS\n    },\n    backend: {\n      loadPath: '/locales/{{lng}}/{{ns}}.json',\n    },\n    ns: ['common', 'medical', 'abha'],\n    defaultNS: 'common',\n    detection: {\n      order: ['localStorage', 'navigator'],\n      caches: ['localStorage'],\n    },\n  });\n\n// Dynamic language attribute for accessibility\ni18n.on('languageChanged', (lng) => {\n  document.documentElement.lang = lng;\n  document.documentElement.setAttribute('dir', 'ltr');\n});\n\nexport default i18n;\n```\n\n### Translation Dictionary Examples:\n- **English (`/locales/en/medical.json`)**:\n  - `\"prescription\"`: \"Prescription\"\n  - `\"lab_report\"`: \"Lab Investigation Report\"\n  - `\"dosage\"`: \"Dosage\"\n  - `\"after_food\"`: \"After Meals\"\n  - `\"before_food\"`: \"Before Meals\"\n  - `\"abnormal_flag\"`: \"Abnormal Result\"\n- **Hindi (`/locales/hi/medical.json`)**:\n  - `\"prescription\"`: \"डॉक्टर की पर्ची / नुस्खा\"\n  - `\"lab_report\"`: \"जांच रिपोर्ट\"\n  - `\"dosage\"`: \"खुराक\"\n  - `\"after_food\"`: \"खाने के बाद\"\n  - `\"before_food\"`: \"खाने से पहले\"\n  - `\"abnormal_flag\"`: \"असामान्य परिणाम\"\n\n---\n\n## 9. QR Code Generation in React (`qrcode.react`)\n\nFor patient ABHA ID cards and hospital desk scan-and-share:\n\n```tsx\nimport React, { useRef } from 'react';\nimport { QRCodeSVG, QRCodeCanvas } from 'qrcode.react';\nimport { Download } from 'lucide-react';\n\ninterface AbhaQrProps {\n  abhaNumber: string;\n  abhaAddress: string;\n  fullName: string;\n  gender: string;\n  dob: string;\n}\n\nexport const AbhaQrCard: React.FC<AbhaQrProps> = ({ abhaNumber, abhaAddress, fullName, gender, dob }) => {\n  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n\n  // ABDM Standardized Scan-and-Share QR payload format\n  const qrPayload = JSON.stringify({\n    hidn: abhaNumber,\n    hid: abhaAddress,\n    name: fullName,\n    gender: gender,\n    dob: dob,\n  });\n\n  const downloadQrPng = () => {\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current?.querySelector('canvas');\n    if (!canvas) return;\n    const url = canvas.toDataURL('image/png');\n    const a = document.createElement('a');\n    a.href = url;\n    a.download = `ABHA_QR_${abhaAddress.replace('@', '_')}.png`;\n    a.click();\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex flex-col items-center p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200\">\n      <div className=\"p-3 bg-white border border-slate-100 rounded-xl shadow-inner\">\n        {/* Render responsive vector SVG for crisp UI display */}\n        <QRCodeSVG\n          value={qrPayload}\n          size={200}\n          level=\"H\"\n          title={`ABHA QR Code for ${fullName}`}\n          imageSettings={{\n            src: '/abdm-symbol.svg',\n            x: undefined,\n            y: undefined,\n            height: 36,\n            width: 36,\n            excavate: true,\n          }}\n        />\n      </div>\n\n      {/* Hidden canvas for high-resolution PNG download */}\n      <div ref={canvasRef} className=\"hidden\">\n        <QRCodeCanvas value={qrPayload} size={600} level=\"H\" />\n      </div>\n\n      <button\n        onClick={downloadQrPng}\n        className=\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-sky-700 bg-sky-50 rounded-lg hover:bg-sky-100 transition-colors\"\n      >\n        <Download className=\"w-4 h-4\" /> Download QR\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Web Speech API for Voice Input in Browsers\n\nAllows doctors or patients to dictate symptoms, medical histories, or notes in Hindi or English:\n\n```tsx\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from 'react';\nimport { Mic, MicOff } from 'lucide-react';\n\ninterface VoiceInputProps {\n  language: 'en-IN' | 'hi-IN';\n  onTranscript: (text: string) => void;\n}\n\nexport const VoiceInputButton: React.FC<VoiceInputProps> = ({ language, onTranscript }) => {\n  const [isListening, setIsListening] = useState(false);\n  const [supported, setSupported] = useState(true);\n  const recognitionRef = useRef<any>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const SpeechRecognition =\n      (window as any).SpeechRecognition || (window as any).webkitSpeechRecognition;\n\n    if (!SpeechRecognition) {\n      setSupported(false);\n      return;\n    }\n\n    const recognition = new SpeechRecognition();\n    recognition.continuous = true;\n    recognition.interimResults = true;\n    recognition.lang = language;\n\n    recognition.onresult = (event: any) => {\n      let finalTranscript = '';\n      for (let i = event.resultIndex; i < event.results.length; i++) {\n        if (event.results[i].isFinal) {\n          finalTranscript += event.results[i][0].transcript + ' ';\n        }\n      }\n      if (finalTranscript) {\n        onTranscript(finalTranscript.trim());\n      }\n    };\n\n    recognition.onerror = () => setIsListening(false);\n    recognition.onend = () => setIsListening(false);\n\n    recognitionRef.current = recognition;\n\n    return () => {\n      if (recognitionRef.current) recognitionRef.current.abort();\n    };\n  }, [language, onTranscript]);\n\n  const toggleListening = () => {\n    if (!recognitionRef.current) return;\n    if (isListening) {\n      recognitionRef.current.stop();\n      setIsListening(false);\n    } else {\n      recognitionRef.current.start();\n      setIsListening(true);\n    }\n  };\n\n  if (!supported) return null;\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      type=\"button\"\n      onClick={toggleListening}\n      aria-label={isListening ? 'Stop voice recording' : 'Start voice recording'}\n      className={`p-2.5 rounded-full transition-all ${\n        isListening\n          ? 'bg-red-500 text-white animate-pulse shadow-lg shadow-red-200'\n          : 'bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-200'\n      }`}\n    >\n      {isListening ? <MicOff className=\"w-5 h-5\" /> : <Mic className=\"w-5 h-5\" />}\n    </button>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. Supabase Schema Design Patterns for Health Records (PostgreSQL + RLS)\n\nBelow is the production-ready SQL migration pattern conforming to PostgreSQL RLS and FHIR R4:\n\n```sql\n-- Enable necessary extensions\nCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS \"uuid-ossp\";\nCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS \"pgcrypto\";\n\n-- 1. Profiles Table (Linked to Supabase Auth)\nCREATE TABLE public.profiles (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  abha_number VARCHAR(17) UNIQUE,       -- Format: 91-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX\n  abha_address VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE,     -- Format: name@sbx / name@abdm\n  full_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  gender VARCHAR(10) CHECK (gender IN ('MALE', 'FEMALE', 'OTHER')),\n  date_of_birth DATE NOT NULL,\n  blood_group VARCHAR(5),               -- 'A+', 'B+', 'O+', etc.\n  phone_number VARCHAR(15),\n  emergency_contact JSONB,             -- { name: \"...\", relation: \"...\", phone: \"...\" }\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),\n  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 2. Care Contexts (ABDM Encounter representation)\nCREATE TABLE public.care_contexts (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  patient_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  reference_number VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL, -- e.g., OPD-2026-09-001\n  display_name TEXT NOT NULL,           -- e.g., \"Consultation with Dr. Sharma\"\n  facility_name TEXT NOT NULL,          -- e.g., \"Apollo Clinics, Bengaluru\"\n  facility_hfr_id VARCHAR(50),          -- Health Facility Registry ID\n  encounter_date TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 3. Health Records (Prescriptions, Diagnostic Reports, Discharge Summaries)\nCREATE TABLE public.health_records (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  patient_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  care_context_id UUID REFERENCES public.care_contexts(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,\n  record_type VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL CHECK (\n    record_type IN ('PRESCRIPTION', 'DIAGNOSTIC_REPORT', 'DISCHARGE_SUMMARY', 'IMMUNIZATION')\n  ),\n  title TEXT NOT NULL,\n  doctor_name TEXT,\n  doctor_registration_no TEXT,          -- e.g., NMC / State council registration\n  record_date DATE NOT NULL,\n  document_url TEXT,                   -- Supabase storage path\n  raw_ocr_text TEXT,                    -- Extracted OCR transcript\n  fhir_bundle JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb, -- NRCeS FHIR R4 Bundle\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),\n  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 4. Medications Table (Normalized view of prescription medicines)\nCREATE TABLE public.prescriptions_medications (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  record_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.health_records(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  medicine_name TEXT NOT NULL,          -- e.g., \"Dolo 650mg Tablet\"\n  generic_name TEXT,                    -- e.g., \"Paracetamol\"\n  dosage_form VARCHAR(30),              -- 'Tablet', 'Syrup', 'Capsule', 'Injection'\n  frequency VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,       -- '1-0-1', '0-1-0', '1-1-1', 'SOS', 'OD', 'BD'\n  timing VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL,          -- 'AFTER_FOOD', 'BEFORE_FOOD', 'WITH_FOOD'\n  duration_days INT NOT NULL,\n  instructions TEXT,\n  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n\n-- 5. Lab Observations (Normalized view for metric trend tracking like HbA1c, Cholesterol)\nCREATE TABLE public.lab_observations (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  record_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.health_records(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  patient_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  test_name TEXT NOT NULL,              -- e.g., \"HbA1c\", \"Fasting Blood Sugar\"\n  loinc_code VARCHAR(20),               -- Standard LOINC code (e.g. 4548-4)\n  value NUMERIC NOT NULL,\n  unit VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,            -- e.g., \"%\", \"mg/dL\"\n  reference_low NUMERIC,\n  reference_high NUMERIC,\n  flag VARCHAR(10) CHECK (flag IN ('NORMAL', 'LOW', 'HIGH', 'CRITICAL')),\n  observed_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL\n);\n\n-- Indexing for performance\nCREATE INDEX idx_health_records_patient ON public.health_records(patient_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_lab_obs_patient_test ON public.lab_observations(patient_id, test_name);\nCREATE INDEX idx_health_records_fhir ON public.health_records USING GIN(fhir_bundle);\n\n-- 6. Strict Row-Level Security (RLS) Policies\nALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE public.care_contexts ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE public.health_records ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE public.prescriptions_medications ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\nALTER TABLE public.lab_observations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;\n\n-- Note: Wrap auth.uid() in (SELECT auth.uid()) for optimal Postgres plan caching\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can view their own profile\"\n  ON public.profiles FOR SELECT\n  TO authenticated\n  USING (id = (SELECT auth.uid()));\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can update their own profile\"\n  ON public.profiles FOR UPDATE\n  TO authenticated\n  USING (id = (SELECT auth.uid()));\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can view their own health records\"\n  ON public.health_records FOR SELECT\n  TO authenticated\n  USING (patient_id = (SELECT auth.uid()));\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can insert their own health records\"\n  ON public.health_records FOR INSERT\n  TO authenticated\n  WITH CHECK (patient_id = (SELECT auth.uid()));\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can delete their own health records\"\n  ON public.health_records FOR DELETE\n  TO authenticated\n  USING (patient_id = (SELECT auth.uid()));\n\nCREATE POLICY \"Users can view their own lab results\"\n  ON public.lab_observations FOR SELECT\n  TO authenticated\n  USING (patient_id = (SELECT auth.uid()));\n\n-- Storage Bucket Policies for 'medical-documents' (Private Bucket)\n-- In Supabase dashboard: create bucket 'medical-documents' with public = false.\nCREATE POLICY \"Patient can access own uploaded medical files\"\n  ON storage.objects FOR ALL\n  TO authenticated\n  USING (bucket_id = 'medical-documents' AND (storage.foldername(name))[1] = (SELECT auth.uid())::text)\n  WITH CHECK (bucket_id = 'medical-documents' AND (storage.foldername(name))[1] = (SELECT auth.uid())::text);\n```\n\n---\n\n## 12. Realistic Indian Health Record Mock Data\n\nTo ensure realistic testing, mock datasets should mirror authentic Indian clinical conventions:\n\n### Patient Profile:\n- **Name**: Rajesh V. Sharma\n- **ABHA ID**: `91-4521-8934-7120`\n- **ABHA Address**: `rajesh.sharma@sbx`\n- **Age / Gender**: 54 Y / Male\n- **Blood Group**: B+\n- **Phone**: `+91 98450 12345`\n\n### Prescription 1 (Chronic Care - Hypertension & T2D):\n- **Doctor**: Dr. Suresh Venkatesh, MD (Internal Medicine) — Reg: KMC-45129\n- **Facility**: Manipal Hospital, HAL Airport Road, Bengaluru\n- **Medications**:\n  1. *Glycomet-GP 1 Forte* (Metformin 500mg + Glimepiride 1mg) — `1-0-1` (Morning & Night, Before Food) — 30 Days\n  2. *Telma 40* (Telmisartan 40mg) — `1-0-0` (Morning, After Food) — 30 Days\n  3. *Rosuvas 10* (Rosuvastatin 10mg) — `0-0-1` (Bedtime, After Food) — 30 Days\n\n### Diagnostic Lab Report (Comprehensive Metabolic Panel):\n- **Laboratory**: Lal PathLabs, Indiranagar Branch\n- **Test Observations**:\n  1. `Fasting Blood Sugar (FBS)`: **154 mg/dL** [Ref: 70–99] -> Flag: `HIGH`\n  2. `HbA1c (Glycated Hemoglobin)`: **8.2%** [Ref: 4.0–5.6%] -> Flag: `HIGH`\n  3. `Serum Creatinine`: **1.05 mg/dL** [Ref: 0.7–1.3] -> Flag: `NORMAL`\n  4. `Total Cholesterol`: **228 mg/dL** [Ref: < 200] -> Flag: `HIGH`\n  5. `Triglycerides`: **195 mg/dL** [Ref: < 150] -> Flag: `HIGH`\n\n### NRCeS Compliant FHIR R4 Minimal Bundle Structure:\n```json\n{\n  \"resourceType\": \"Bundle\",\n  \"id\": \"bundle-prescription-001\",\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"versionId\": \"1\",\n    \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-09-20T10:30:00Z\",\n    \"profile\": [\n      \"https://nrces.in/ndhm/fhir/r4/StructureDefinition/PrescriptionRecord\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"identifier\": {\n    \"system\": \"https://manipal.health.in/prescription\",\n    \"value\": \"RX-2026-98124\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"document\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-20T10:30:00Z\",\n  \"entry\": [\n    {\n      \"fullUrl\": \"Composition/comp-01\",\n      \"resource\": {\n        \"resourceType\": \"Composition\",\n        \"status\": \"final\",\n        \"type\": {\n          \"coding\": [\n            {\n              \"system\": \"https://projectndhm.in/fhir/ndhm/CodeSystem/ndhm-document-types\",\n              \"code\": \"PRE\",\n              \"display\": \"Prescription record\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        \"subject\": {\n          \"reference\": \"Patient/rajesh-sharma\",\n          \"display\": \"Rajesh V. Sharma (ABHA: 91-4521-8934-7120)\"\n        },\n        \"author\": [\n          {\n            \"reference\": \"Practitioner/dr-suresh\",\n            \"display\": \"Dr. Suresh Venkatesh (KMC-45129)\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 13. Critical Gotchas, Edge Cases & Practical Considerations\n\n1. **Tailwind CSS v4 Configuration Gotcha**:\n   - Do **not** create a `tailwind.config.js` or `postcss.config.js`. Doing so can cause build warnings or conflicts in v4.\n   - Do **not** use `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;`. Use `@import \"tailwindcss\";` exclusively.\n   - Theme variables and fonts belong inside `@theme { ... }` in your primary CSS file.\n\n2. **Supabase RLS Evaluation Overhead**:\n   - In Supabase RLS policies, never write `auth.uid() = patient_id` directly without parentheses. Write `patient_id = (SELECT auth.uid())`. The `(SELECT ...)` wrapper signals PostgreSQL to evaluate the auth identity once per query rather than re-evaluating it for every individual row, preventing massive query latency on large tables.\n\n3. **Tesseract.js WASM & Memory Bottlenecks**:\n   - Tesseract’s WASM binary and language traineddata (`eng.traineddata`, `hin.traineddata`) weigh 5MB–15MB.\n   - Always terminate idle workers using `await worker.terminate()` to prevent memory leaks in mobile browsers.\n   - Show a clear visual progress bar; never freeze the UI during processing.\n\n4. **Web Speech API Browser Inconsistencies**:\n   - Chrome on Desktop and Android has full support, but Safari iOS and Firefox have limited or no `SpeechRecognition` support.\n   - Always feature-detect:\n     ```typescript\n     const isSpeechSupported = 'SpeechRecognition' in window || 'webkitSpeechRecognition' in window;\n     ```\n   - Provide standard text input / keyboard fallbacks when `isSpeechSupported` is false.\n   - Hindi speech recognition (`hi-IN`) requires an active internet connection on Chrome, as transcription is routed to Google's speech servers.\n\n5. **ABDM Sandbox Gateway vs. Production Protocol**:\n   - In Sandbox (`dev.abdm.gov.in`), session tokens are fetched with `grantType: \"client_credentials\"`.\n   - Never initiate direct browser-to-gateway calls due to CORS restrictions on ABDM endpoints and the exposure of your client credentials. Always invoke ABDM APIs through your Supabase Edge Functions.\n   - Sandbox health IDs frequently expire or reset during testing cycles; build a mock fallback mode in development so frontend development is never blocked by sandbox downtime.\n\n6. **DPDP Act 2023 (Digital Personal Data Protection) Compliance**:\n   - In India, health records are classified as sensitive personal data.\n   - Mask Aadhaar details everywhere (only display `XXXX-XXXX-1234`).\n   - Store medical images in private Supabase buckets with signed URLs that expire within 5–15 minutes, rather than using permanent public URLs.\n","Recipient":"f5f2b675-7cd6-4dd4-a9e0-d982427a0678","toolAction":"Sending research report to parent","toolSummary":"Send research findings"}}]}
